    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0431" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/2762½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">17 September, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: It occurs to me to
                    request you to make pointed inquiry of the British, French, and Italian
                    governments as to what the so-called Allied Military Council at Vladivostok is,
                    of <pb facs="0432" n="386" xml:id="pg386"/> whom it is composed, and by whose
                    authority it was formed and is undertaking to act, intimating at the same time
                    that we recognize the authority of no such body and would be very glad to have
                    the situation at Vladivostok cleared of unnecessary complications.</p>
                <p>Cordially and faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
